<title>USA: Conn. Gov seeks $500 mln in GO bonds FY 98 and 99.</title>
<headline>Conn. Gov seeks $500 mln in GO bonds FY 98 and 99.</headline>
<dateline>HARTFORD 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Connecticut Gov. John Rowland on Thursday proposed general obligation authorizations at about $500 million in fiscal years 1998 and 1999.</p>
<p>Rowland, a Republican, said in documents issued with his budget speech that he continued his efforts to limit capital bonding.</p>
<p>--Hartford newsroom (860) 727-0224</p>
